00:00:34.591 --> 00:00:38.583
in order to move a step closer towards

00:00:38.583 --> 00:00:42.760
doing something that you actually love?

00:00:42.760 --> 00:00:44.150
- So it's a really interesting question

00:00:44.150 --> 00:00:45.070
and as I was listening,

00:00:45.070 --> 00:00:46.475
and I hope people were paying attention.

00:00:46.475 --> 00:00:51.475
Most people spend money on dumb things

00:00:54.430 --> 00:00:57.233
which then forces them to
do things they don't want.

00:00:58.650 --> 00:01:01.550
So step number one for
most people in here.

00:01:01.550 --> 00:01:03.700
They should sell their home,

00:01:03.700 --> 00:01:05.823
take the money and go rent.

00:01:07.697 --> 00:01:12.697
They should return their
BMW and get a Toyota.

00:01:14.525 --> 00:01:16.619
- [Man] I own a BMW. It's not that bad.

00:01:16.619 --> 00:01:20.000
- And honestly, that
becomes the vulnerability.

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:21.771
Why do you own a BMW?

00:01:21.771 --> 00:01:22.781
- [Man] Because I love the car,

00:01:22.781 --> 00:01:23.873
'cause the branding,

00:01:23.873 --> 00:01:25.043
I love driving it.

00:01:25.043 --> 00:01:26.080
So I don't know.

00:01:26.080 --> 00:01:28.520
- So to me that's where it
gets interesting, right?

00:01:28.520 --> 00:01:30.970
Do you or do you like what the brand does

00:01:30.970 --> 00:01:33.020
to make you look to other people?

00:01:33.020 --> 00:01:35.210
I don't know. I'm not
assuming. I don't know.

00:01:35.210 --> 00:01:36.190
- [Man] You have a
point. You have a point.

00:01:36.190 --> 00:01:37.023
- I know I have a point.

00:01:37.023 --> 00:01:39.510
I don't know you, but I know in the macro

00:01:39.510 --> 00:01:42.938
that 98% of people that
buy a Mercedes or BMW

00:01:42.938 --> 00:01:46.200
likes what it makes other
people think of them,

00:01:46.200 --> 00:01:49.285
not that they like it
and that $487 a month

00:01:49.285 --> 00:01:52.535
